    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based rule for membership level 4 in `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipLevel` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`).\n\n**Change:** The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are now explicitly capped at level 3. Level 4 is then granted only when the owner's tenure \u2014 days elapsed since `registrationDate` \u2014 exceeds 365:\n\n```java\nlevel = Math.min(level, 3);\nLocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();\nif (registrationDate != null && ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365) {\n    level++;\n}\nreturn level;\n```\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is the current day (zero tenure), the tenure bump never fires for a new owner, so a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` of 0, and a 3-member household lands at level 3 \u2014 not 4. The household plays no part in scoring; the pre-tenure factors max out at 3 from email + unique name alone, matching the spec and test narration.\n\nI also added the `java.time.LocalDate` / `ChronoUnit` imports and updated the Javadoc to describe the 1\u20134 range and the tenure rule.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` case asserting level 3 passes).",
